cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  Public domain (CC0). Citing is a courtesy to your readers, not to us — pin the
  version tag and the commit, because main moves daily. Cite it as what it is:
  model legislation, a research draft, never enacted law. Cite a provision by
  section and link by line: model_act_v3_4.txt#L236 opens SEC. 4; the section-to-line
  index is in the README. Every authority the draft relies on is listed, with the
  proposition each is cited for, in standards/table_of_authorities.md.
title: "Model Act — Frontier AI Public Welfare Offenses"
abstract: >-
  A public-domain model state criminal statute applying the responsible corporate
  officer doctrine — United States v. Dotterweich, 320 U.S. 277 (1943), and United
  States v. Park, 421 U.S. 658 (1975) — to frontier artificial intelligence:
  personal, non-delegable duties for the officers of developers of models trained
  above a bracketed 10^26-operation threshold. Fourteen sections (SEC. 0–13) with
  drafting notes, draft implementing regulations, a complete public drafting record
  including a hostile brief built against the text, and an append-only register of
  the project's own errata. Drafted in public by one maintainer with AI assistance
  disclosed. Never enacted; no completed review is claimed.
type: software
version: "3.4"
date-released: "2026-08-19"
